// Remote video of a simulator (later, browser) pane: H.264 from the helper
// that owns the pixels (ADR-0012). Replies MediaTicket.
//
// Over QUIC (the default): connect to the host's address (the one this
// connection uses) at quic_port, ALPN "hmk-media/1", the same pinned
// certificate; open a bidirectional stream and send the 32-byte ticket.
// On that stream the client then sends records: u8 1 + u32 seq (a frame
// received whole), or u8 2 (send a keyframe: the decoder lost its place).
// Each frame arrives on its own server-initiated unidirectional stream: a
// 17-byte header (u32 seq, u8 flags (1 keyframe, 2 refresh, 4 HEVC, 8
// cropped), u64 capture time µs, u16 width, u16 height), when cropped the
// part of the display it shows (u16 x, y, w, h, each a fraction × 65535),
// then the frame to the end of the stream. A stream
// reset by the server is a frame given up; the next frame shown is a
// keyframe.
//
// In band (in_band): frames come as MediaFrame messages on this
// connection and are acked with MediaAck. A guest's daemon passes frames to
// its app this way; it's the path a relay would take.
//
// Data, all big-endian. Frames are AVCC (4-byte NAL lengths); keyframes lead
// with their SPS and PPS. The session ends with this connection, CloseMedia,
// or the pane (MediaEnded).
